      <h2>Does GMT to HKT Change the Date?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Yes. Because HKT is 8 hours ahead of GMT, evening hours in GMT roll into the next calendar day in Hong Kong.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Any GMT time occurring between 16:00 (4:00 PM GMT) and 23:59 (11:59 PM GMT) falls after midnight local time in Hong Kong, advancing the HKT calendar date by +1 day.
      </p>

      <h3>Date Transition Breakdown</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li><strong>GMT 00:00 to 15:59:</strong> Results in HKT 08:00 to 23:59 on the <strong>SAME calendar date</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>GMT 16:00:</strong> Results in HKT 00:00 (midnight) on the <strong>NEXT calendar date</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>GMT 18:00:</strong> Results in HKT 02:00 AM on the <strong>NEXT calendar date</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>GMT 21:00:</strong> Results in HKT 05:00 AM on the <strong>NEXT calendar date</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

