        <li><strong>Malaysia Time (MYT):</strong> Shares UTC+8. Used in Kuala Lumpur and Malaysia.</li>
        <li><strong>Central Indonesia Time (WITA):</strong> Shares UTC+8. Used in Bali and Makassar. Compare with <a href="/gmt-to-wib/" style="color: var(--accent);">GMT to WIB</a> (UTC+7).</li>
        <li><strong>Japan Standard Time (JST):</strong> Operates at UTC+9 (1 hour ahead of HKT).</li>
        <li><strong>Korea Standard Time (KST):</strong> Operates at UTC+9 (1 hour ahead of HKT).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In software programming and database design, always specify <code>Asia/Hong_Kong</code> rather than assuming generic regional aliases.
      </p>
